summary:
- topic: Board Member Recognition
  text: 'Board: The board honored departing member Jennifer Kiley for her service,
    particularly her significant time commitment to the city''s 2040 Comprehensive
    Plan Committee. They also nominated Molly Shen for Board Chair and T-Ann Ratliff
    for Vice Chair for the upcoming term.'
- topic: Student Initiatives & Recognition
  text: 'Students: Student representative Elliot reported on positive school events,
    including a "Day of Welcome" at Brown School. Student Huck Charv presented his
    self-started "Study Abroad Scholarship" to address equity issues, raising over
    $1,200 to help financially disadvantaged students participate in foreign exchange
    trips, which received strong praise from the board.'
- topic: 'Superintendent''s Report: Staff Recognition & Snow Day Policy'
  text: 'Administration: The Superintendent recognized staff veterans, Education Support
    Professionals (Ed Techs), and substitute teachers for their critical contributions.
    He also announced a new snow day policy, eliminating remote learning days for
    the first five snow days and adding them to the end of the school year, citing
    that remote days are not a good fit for the youngest learners.'
- topic: Facilities and Graduation Venue
  text: 'Administration/Board: Following the failure of the athletic complex referendum,
    the administration will pause and research before bringing it back to the board.
    A discussion was held about moving the high school graduation from the stadium,
    due to weather and field condition issues, to a larger venue to allow more family
    members to attend. The board supported surveying families and students for input.'
- topic: Teacher Union Response to Snow Day Policy
  text: 'Teachers (SPTA): The South Portland Teacher Association (SPTA) representatives
    expressed concern over the change in the snow day policy. They argued that staff
    had made plans based on the previously approved calendar and the recent practice
    of using remote days, and they urged the board to collaborate with educators to
    create a more equitable and effective plan for inclement weather days.'
- topic: Public Comment on Mental Health
  text: 'Citizens: A citizen thanked the district for its continued focus on student
    mental health, highlighting the improved communication and resources provided
    to families, such as the 988 crisis number on new student IDs.'
- topic: Service Employees Contract Ratification
  text: 'Board/Administration: The board ratified the three-year contract (FY25-27)
    with the South Portland School District Service Employees Association (SPESPA).
    Both the board''s negotiating team and the superintendent praised the collaborative
    and professional nature of the negotiations.'
